================================================================================================
CONTROLS
================================================================================================
A. least realizer vs larger lifts in the SAME exact realizer class.
   The word, R-profile, episode structure, W_i and eta_i of the shared prefix
   are class invariants; the absolute seed and entry heights are not.
   prefix of 285175, N=12: word=(1, 1, 3, 2, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1), S=16, class = 23031 mod 131072
             lift  word matches  R-profile id    W over prefix  log2 m_0
            23031          True          True      8.603527014   14.4913
           154103          True          True      8.603527014   17.2335
           285175          True          True      8.603527014   18.1215
           416247          True          True      8.603527014   18.6671
           547319          True          True      8.603527014   19.0620
   => occupation/W/eta of the prefix are IDENTICAL across lifts while log2 m_0
      grows without bound.  Any charge containing log2 m_0 is therefore not a
      function of the prefix, which is precisely Remark 13.3's mechanism.

B. long all-ones prefixes (zero-confined, positively realizable at finite depth).
     k least realizer 2^(k+1)-1  #leading d=1       R_k   W over [0,k)    mean z
     4                       31             4   -2.3399       2.407407  0.601852
     8                      511             8   -4.6797       2.882945  0.360368
    12                     8191            12   -7.0196       2.976878  0.248073
    16                   131071            16   -9.3594       2.995433  0.187215
    20                  2097151            20  -11.6993       2.999098  0.149955
   => mean corridor weight stays O(1) while the least realizer is 2^{k+1}-1:
      height is in the accounting, and small mean weight does not make an
      episode cheap in seed scale.

C. the Prop. 13.2 oscillator: digit 2 inside the corridor, digit 1 outside.
   c=0: 1 episodes in [0,200), lengths [200], occupation 200, max gap 1
   c=1: 1 episodes in [0,200), lengths [200], occupation 200, max gap 1
   => many short episodes; episode COUNT is unbounded (Prop. 13.2) so no
      bound of the form P <= const can exist.  Consistent with A above.

D. the -1 all-ones trajectory (negative control).
   -1 is a fixed point of T(x)=(3x+1)/2: d=1 forever, R_n = n(1-alpha) -> -inf,
   so EVERY n is occupied for every c >= 0: one infinite episode, O_c = infinity.
   It satisfies the corridor condition with no positivity: the hypothesis the
   argument needs is m_n >= 1 (used in Bcal_a >= m_0 and in m_n >= m_0 2^-c),
   i.e. POSITIVITY OF THE STATES, not positivity of the seed alone.

E. affine recurrence over positive reals, no integer ray.
   Fix the word of 285175 and run x_{n+1} = (3 x_n + 1)/2^{d_n} from real x_0:
     x_0=   2.852e+05 -> x_40=        751841   (integer orbit m_40 = 751841)
     x_0=         0.5 -> x_40=        43.034   (integer orbit m_40 = 751841)
     x_0=       1e+06 -> x_40=   2.63632e+06   (integer orbit m_40 = 751841)
     x_0=       1e-06 -> x_40=       41.7159   (integer orbit m_40 = 751841)
   The R-profile is prescribed by the word, so corridor membership, W_i and
   eta_i are IDENTICAL for every real x_0.  Any argument that never uses
   integrality or m_n >= 1 is valid here too and therefore proves nothing
   arithmetic.  Proposition J uses Bcal_a >= m_0 (i.e. C_a > 0), which holds
   for every positive real start, and the entry lemma, which is purely
   symbolic -- so J is NOT an integer obstruction.  Recorded as such.

